{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 170, :comments ["<b>Let my supplication come</b> — [as in] בהתחננו אלינו (Genesis 42:21), [meaning] 'when he pleaded with us'; thus [here] תחנתי is 'my plea.'"], :book :psalms, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 119, :notes {0 "The comment parses תחנתי as related to the root חנן (to plead/seek favor), citing Genesis 42:21 as a parallel; 'בצרתה לי' appears to be an idiom meaning 'it is clear/evident to me,' affirming the reading."}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Psalms -- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/he-il/tanach/parshanut_hamikra/full-text/eben-ezra/tehilim"] ["Wikisource Mikraot Gedolot" "http://en.wikisource.org/wiki/Mikraot_Gedolot/"] ["Tanakh, Venice, 1617-1619" "https://dlib.rsl.ru/viewer/01007514045#?page=4"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:41:02.885510119Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}